+## 3.2.0
+
+Deterministic docs operational graph: a new canonical module
+(`canonical/docs/.og/`) that indexes every project doc into a local SQLite
+database and computes its relationships, with zero added runtime
+dependencies beyond Node's built-in `node:sqlite`.
+
+- **New canonical package `docs/.og/`** — `cli.mjs` (`build()`/`index()`/
+  `reindex()`/`query()`/`search()`/`list()`/`unedge()`), `constants.mjs`,
+  `utils.mjs`, `docs.mjs`, `edges.mjs`, `schema.mjs`, plus `cli.test.mjs`
+  (never copied into a bootstrapped project) and a schema-initialized seed
+  `.sqlite`. ID assignment is additive-only, idempotent, and collision-safe;
+  edges cover six authored graduation types plus computed `mirrors-*` and
+  automatic `keyword-match` relations; `build()` also emits a generated
+  Mermaid mindmap artifact.
+- **New `reindex-graph` route** (`references/reindex-graph.md`) — rebuilds
+  the operational graph standalone, without a full `launch` run: Step 0
+  idempotently deploys/refreshes the six module files, then a deterministic
+  build followed by a 3-phase intelligent scan (fulfill frontmatter, rebuild
+  edges from the now-complete table, review/retract stale relations).
+  `launch`'s own Materialize stage (`references/launch/01d-launch-graph-verify.md`,
+  replacing the old `01d-launch-verify.md`) now delegates to it wholesale
+  instead of duplicating the copy logic.
+- **Dev/design lifecycle wiring** — `dev/references/01-context-gathering.md`
+  and `design/references/01-context-gathering.md`/`04-research.md` query the
+  graph on the read path (required grep/glob fallback); `dev/references/06-document.md`
+  and `design/references/09-publish.md` call `index()` non-blockingly on the
+  write path when a doc graduates.
+- `Documentation/01 Principles.md` — new frontmatter rule: quote `purpose:`
+  in double quotes whenever it contains a YAML-reserved character, so a
+  scan-written value can't break a consuming site's frontmatter parse.
+- Compatible, additive change — no existing command, placeholder, or
+  workflow-step behavior changes; the new module and route are opt-in
+  surface area.
+
